  "worked_solution": "Let's construct our matrix:\n\n- The index $2$ in ${J}_{2}(\\pi )$ means that we have a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The value $\\pi $ in ${J}_{2}(\\pi )$ means that we have $\\pi $'s on the main diagonal.\n\n- Also, we must have $1$'s on the superdiagonal (the diagonal above the main one).\n\nGiven that all the other entries must be zero, our Jordan block is\n\n$$\n{J}_{2}(\\pi )=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi  & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\pi \\end{aligned}].\n$$",
